---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/hareeshagunasekara/iconnook';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The simple rules for using IconNook: free to use, icons keep their own licenses, provided as is."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="section-title">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated: 8 November 2026</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
      IconNook is free for everyone. By using the site you agree to these short terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">The icons</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Every icon belongs to its authors and keeps the license of its icon set, which is shown on
      every icon page. Your use of an icon is governed by that license, including giving credit when
      it asks for it. See{' '}
      <a class="link" href="/licenses">
        Licenses &amp; attribution
      </a>{' '}
      for what each license means.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Logos and brand icons: the license covers the drawing, not the brand. Logos and brand names
      belong to their owners; follow their brand guidelines.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">The website and code</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      IconNook's own code is open source under the Apache License 2.0. Please use the site and its
      API fairly: automated bulk downloading that overloads the service isn't allowed, and requests
      may be rate limited.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">No warranty</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      IconNook and the icons are provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. We work hard to
      label every license correctly, but please check an icon's license before relying on it, and
      tell us if something is wrong.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Problems and takedowns</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you believe an icon is mislabeled or shouldn't be here,{' '}
      <a class="link" href={`${REPO}/issues`}>
        report it on GitHub
      </a>{' '}
      and we'll look into it promptly. Security issues go to{' '}
      <a class="link" href={`${REPO}/security/advisories/new`}>
        a private security report
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
